amendments is included in endnote 5.   Endnotes  Endnote 1—About the endnotes  Australian Broadcasting Corporation (Transitional Provisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 1983  Modifications—Endnote 6 If the compiled law is affected by a modification that is in force, details of the modification are included in endnote 6.  Misdescribed amendments—Endnote 7 An amendment is a misdescribed amendment if the effect of the amendment cannot be incorporated into the text of the compilation. Any misdescribed amendment is included in endnote 7.  Miscellaneous—Endnote 8 Endnote 8 includes any additional information that may be helpful for a reader of the compilation.    Endnotes  Endnote 2—Abbreviation key  Australian Broadcasting Corporation (Transitional Provisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 1983  Endnote 2—Abbreviation key  ad = added or inserted pres = present am = amended prev = previous c = clause(s) (prev) = previously Ch = Chapter(s) Pt = Part(s) def = definition(s) r = regulation(s)/rule(s) Dict = Dictionary Reg = Regulation/Regulations disallowed = disallowed by Parliament reloc = relocated Div = Division(s) renum = renumbered exp = expired or ceased to have effect rep = repealed hdg = heading(s) rs = repealed and substituted LI = Legislative Instrument s = section(s) LIA = Legislative Instruments Act 2003 Sch = Schedule(s) mod = modified/modification Sdiv = Subdivision(s) No = Number(s) SLI = Select Legislative Instrument o = order(s) SR = Statutory Rules Ord = Ordinance Sub-Ch = Sub-Chapter(s) orig = original SubPt = Subpart(s) par = paragraph(s)/subparagraph(s) /sub-subparagraph(s)    Endnotes  Endnote 3—Legislation history  Australian Broadcasting Corporation (Transitional Provisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 1983  Endnote 3—Legislation history  Act Number and year Assent Commencement Application, saving and transitional provisions Australian Broadcasting Corporation (Transitional Provisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 1983 7, 1983" ;
